WEBVTT

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.440
I'm dreaming of that again...

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:55.940
Doctor, as soon as the adjustments are 
complete, send them to the briefing room.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.560
Let's get back to the briefing room.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.400
Yeah.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.450
First you have to take your medicine.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.530
I don't like the medicine. It's bitter.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.460
Okay. I'll talk to the doctor 
and have them give you a shot.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.600
Yeah, I love shots!

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.460
They're not bitter.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:15.680
Yeah.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:17.880
Hey, Cryska.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:18.880
What?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.080
When's our next vacation?

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.010
I want to go see Yuuya!

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:31.020
<b>Dark Recollection</b>

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.200
Damn it!

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:10.990
Yuuya!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.250
These tiny little differences 
are annoying me!

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.260
Yuuya Bridges!

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:33.370
What?

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.230
Sorry, Lieutenant!

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.480
No you don't!

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.130
He was losing the whole time. I'm 
amazed he managed to come back.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.460
The bookies are going to lose a fortune.

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.770
Yuuya won, didn't he?

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.040
You okay?

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:12.260
What do you mean?

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:16.880
What do I mean? You haven't 
even touched your food.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.560
No, that's not true.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:21.680
See?

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.750
Are you sure you're okay?

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:29.740
Yeah... Actually, it's what 
we were talking about earlier.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.290
Um, well... You said you 
wanted something from me.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.250
There's Yuuya!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:38.750
Again?

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.050
What the hell are you doing?

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:46.060
Your face is all red!

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:47.630
I think you want it.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.550
Hey, stop it.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.640
Lt. Cui, this is a public facility.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:53.640
Please act responsibly.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.400
What's your problem, princess?

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.480
We're busy now, so butt out.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:02.360
Yuuya and I are eating.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.190
We Eishi must get proper nutrition.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.480
Don't bother us.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.240
Yuuya, huh?

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:12.120
You're the one who's bothering us.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:16.740
Lt. Cui. You're a little out of line.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.520
Right, right.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:23.550
Got it. A wife needs to 
do what her husband says.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.730
W-Wife?

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:25.630
That's right.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:29.740
You beat me, Yuuya, so you have the 
right to be more than just my lover.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:33.220
This isn't the time to be messing around.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:36.240
What do you mean messing around?

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:39.260
Aren't you fighting the Infinities tomorrow?

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:43.680
Their stealth is a problem, 
but nothing I can't handle.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.740
It's not like they turn 
invisible or anything.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:49.570
If I let them get a shot in and 
see their location, they're mine.

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:51.900
You're underestimating the US military.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.590
Honestly, they're very strong.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:56.270
Thanks for the warning.

00:07:56.270 --> 00:08:01.500
But the United Chinese Front doesn't 
care about the Blue Flag exercises.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.910
They don't matter.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.420
And I don't care about this farce, either.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.420
As long as I get to enjoy a battle against 
strong Eishi, that's enough for me.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:13.430
I see.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.220
So that was it?

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.310
So listen up, Yuuya.

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:23.950
If I win we're going on a honeymoon.

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:25.310
H-Honeymoon?

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:26.720
Yes!

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:29.900
We'll spend the night together in a 
cottage with an amazing view of the lake!

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:32.490
And at night we'll get 
close next to the fire...

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:33.820
Won't that be wonderful?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:38.890
Or what? Do you think I'm going to lose?

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:41.150
No, that's not it.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:46.460
I'm not some floozy who'd let you 
sleep with her over a bad joke.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.090
Now that that's decided I'm going to bed.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.700
I've got to get ready for my honeymoon night!

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:54.720
That's what she's got to get ready for?

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.010
Zai jian!

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.930
Christ... the food's cold now.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:08.910
Lt. Cui's plan for fighting the Infinities.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:10.300
Do you think it'll work?

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.830
She was just giving us the outline.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:15.240
I'm sure she's got a deeper plan.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:19.160
But whatever it is, the US Military's 
probably already accounted for it.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:19.780
Yeah.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.700
The Raptor is amazing at fighting other TSFs.

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:28.290
But I'm not going to lose to the Raptor.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:33.300
I'm going to prove to everyone that 
our Shiranui is the ultimate TSF.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:38.190
What?

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:42.750
No, you just seemed to be 
really enjoying your food.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.430
Yeah.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.940
So you like carrots?

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:00.450
This is pathetic!

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.420
How am I the only one left?

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:14.670
Perfect.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.890
If I'm this close I can see them!

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:30.270
You're too slow!

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:36.620
What?

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:40.360
Bao Feng 1 has taken damage 
in its chest cockpit.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.120
That damage is fatal.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:42.990
Unit destroyed.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:49.420
What is this? We never had a chance!

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:55.380
Damn it all! They're just messing with me...

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.480
Bao Feng has lost 4 units.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:10:59.880
Infinities have lost zero.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:05.550
The Bao Feng Test Flight didn't 
even get a chance to get up close.

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:08.570
So that's the power of stealth?

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:09.890
It's not just the TSFs.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:13.500
They're all pretty good.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.320
Yeah.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.450
Lt. Yifei's flight was wiped 
out in just 4 minutes.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:33.920
They were just screwing with her.

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:35.590
Yuuya!

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:37.920
You guys!

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:39.880
What are you doing here?

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:42.040
It's rare for you both to come see me.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:45.280
Cryska wants to chat with you.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.760
With me?

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:52.190
Yuuya Bridges.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:54.430
There's something I want to ask you.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.330
Aren't there too many people here in town?

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.790
If we're going to discuss something 
in secret, the more people the better.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.840
And the Soviets aren't allowed in town.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:16.670
It's safe, right?

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:20.060
Yeah, that's true.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.550
Inia?

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:22.560
What's wrong?

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.800
No.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:28.350
Why don't we get something to drink?

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:30.220
No, I'm fine.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.710
Don't worry about it.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:34.990
No, that's not the issue.

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:39.860
I'm the one that brought you out here, I 
can't put any additional stress on you.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:42.860
Cryska can actually be pretty nice sometimes.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:47.900
No, she's always trying her best.

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:50.870
But she's just too frank with her 
words, so people misunderstand her.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.690
I bet she wouldn't want to hear it from me.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.300
I used to be the exact same 
until a little while ago.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.080
What's so funny?

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.670
No, nothing.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:11.930
So what did you want to ask me?

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.240
Remember what I said before?

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:19.860
That Inia is particularly interested in you?

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.410
Yeah, it seems so.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.860
I want to know why.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:28.890
Wouldn't it be faster to ask Inia?

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.660
She doesn't know why.That's 
why I've come out here.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.470
I see.

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:36.090
And well...

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:39.040
My own personal issues are involved as well.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.870
Your own issues? What do you mean?

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:45.340
Most likely a similar phenomenon 
to what's happening to Inia.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:49.660
I can't really explain it,

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:54.730
but it seems that I too find something 
in you I don't see in others.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.610
In me?

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:59.720
Yes. In other words, something's strange...

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.770
When I think about you, I can't...

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:06.690
...concentrate.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:10.730
At this rate it's soon 
going to affect my mission.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:12.700
I need to figure out the cause before then.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:14.840
Tell me, Bridges.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.970
What is this?

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.720
Both for Inia and me...

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:21.440
Why are you the only one 
who affects us this way?

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:23.130
It's clear that you're the cause.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.210
Hold on a second.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:32.330
I just want you to tell me.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.470
I don't know what to do...

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:36.970
...anymore.

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:38.980
Hey, Cryska!

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.480
Can I go look over there?

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:44.060
Don't go too far.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:44.860
Okay!

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:51.020
I had a similar experience just a while ago.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:52.450
What? Is that true?

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:56.990
It's common for someone to let their own 
impatience and irritation get the best of them.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:15:01.930
It was a big problem for me when we 
just started developing the 94 Second.

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:03.200
I see.

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:05.760
My superior officer's values and priorities 
were totally different than mine...

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.500
I'm talking about Yui.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:10.800
The more I thought about her the more 
it upset me and the worse things went.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.470
You and Lt. Takamura?

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:14.200
I see.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.560
For example...

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:21.800
Did Lt. Sandek put pressure on you 
to outperform my score at Kamchatka?

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:27.130
I can't give any details, but 
I was told something similar.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.470
I think that's it.

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:31.490
That's the cause?

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.120
Since you were honest with 
me, I'll be honest with you.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:39.050
There've been a lot of times I was 
stubborn about wanting to beat you.

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:43.450
Really? You're just like me?

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:44.490
Yeah.

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:47.800
We're both test pilots. 
That's normal, isn't it?

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:53.800
I don't think I totally 
understand what you said.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.120
But I do feel a little better.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.190
I see. I'm glad to hear that.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.810
Thank you, Bridges.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.430
I'm honored I was able to help.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:07.310
It might actually be the same reason 
that Inia keeps thinking about me.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.930
You two are very similar.

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:11.680
Inia and I are?

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:15.230
I see... so it looks that way to you?

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:18.700
And in a way, you might be like me.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:21.120
Yuuya!

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.200
Cryska!

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:23.420
Let's get going.

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:24.580
Yeah.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.090
Look! They're so pretty!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.480
I see. You like them?

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.050
I'll take these.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:39.450
I'm jealous. A woman on both 
arms and still not enough?

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:40.060
Bridges?

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:41.480
Here.

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.560
Are you sure?

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:44.780
Yeah.

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:46.060
No, but...

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:49.570
It's not for you. I want to do it, is all.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:50.980
Here.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.600
You two are always together,

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.440
so it'd be better if you both 
had the same flowers, right?

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.120
Cryska,

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:01.490
doesn't it make you happy?

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:08.060
This is the second time I've 
ever been given flowers.

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:11.500
Thank you.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.020
Darling!

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:20.670
Lt. Cui!

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:24.860
Why is my husband meeting in 
secret with another woman?

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:26.000
Are you cheating on me already?

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.340
I'm not cheating on you.

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:29.400
And I'm not even your husband!

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.900
And out of all people, you're 
meeting with the Scarlet Twins?

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.690
Now look...

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:41.910
Sorry, we're talking about 
something important right now!

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:40.540
This pain, this feeling in my chest...

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:42.590
He says it's simple irritation?

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:44.660
Cryska?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:50.000
Ensign Bridges, we'll be leaving.

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:51.920
Wait.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.690
Bye, Yuuya!

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:57.080
Darling!

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:03.100
What the hell was that for?

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.920
Remember this, Yuuya:

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:08.910
Next time you talk to me, don't be
 thinking about another woman, got it?

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.850
What are you talking about?

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:13.610
And...

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:18.610
I couldn't keep our 
promise. I'm really sorry.

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:23.180
The honeymoon? Never thought 
about it, honestly.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.660
That's right.

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:28.620
If it doesn't bother you, 
then it doesn't matter right?

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.630
Are you...?

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:34.590
Of course I'm not crying!

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:40.220
I'm sorry!

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.760
I thought you could dodge 
it if you'd seen it before.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:47.760
First Ensign Barchenowa, and now Lt. Cui?

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.640
Come on, Yuuya! You're not that badly hurt!

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:55.240
What am I doing?

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:08.350
Another.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:10.960
That's pretty impressive, 
getting drunk off orange juice.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.670
Did something happen?

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:18.270
Are those carrots?

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:21.710
Are you going to make some homemade 
cooking for your boyfriend,

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:23.130
like you did before?

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:25.640
Am I right?

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:30.280
Welcome.

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:32.020
Oh, speak of the devil.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:33.770
Lieutenant!

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:38.190
It's rare to see you here.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.050
Are you alone?

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:42.010
No, um, well...

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:44.110
Sir, your order?

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:46.320
The usual.

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:48.540
I'm tired today.

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:51.540
I need a drink, damn it.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.290
I bet.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.690
Come to think of it,

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:58.550
I said I wanted your help with 
something earlier, remember?

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:01.790
Yeah, you did.

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:04.760
You did, come to think of it.

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:11.050
Actually, well...

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:14.560
I want you to teach me 
Japanese sword fighting.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.930
Movement patterns a pilot memorizes

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:20.650
can have a big effect on the indirect 
thought control systems of a TSF.

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:24.190
So if I learn sword fighting, 
the Shiranui can be even...

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:26.030
You don't like Japan,

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:28.410
but that doesn't matter as long 
as there's a girl involved?

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:32.090
That's a pretty convenient policy to have.

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:34.960
Excuse me.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:40.700
I am Ensign Leon Kuze of the US 
65th Combat Training Battalion.

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:44.890
Lt. Takamura Yui of the XFJ plan.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:46.750
You were splendid in today's exercise.

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:49.000
Both your TSF and your own talents.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.240
I'm honored.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:54.180
As a Japanese-American, I'm looking forward 
to fighting the TSF you've developed.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:59.920
But I'm sure it must be difficult to 
develop your TSF with such a handicap.

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:01.150
Handicap?

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.070
I'm leaving.

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:07.120
Get your filthy hand off me.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:11.580
It must've been a lot easier pretending to be a nice
 guy where nobody knew your past.

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:12.840
Hey.

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:14.910
Cut the crap, rich boy.

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:18.270
I'm about to tell them one 
of your old war stories.

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:19.080
Don't run away.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.300
I said let me go!

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:24.720
Why you-

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:31.530
Stop it, both of you!

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.850
I figured that was going to happen.

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:35.480
Who are you?

00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:39.960
Sharon Imes of the 65th 
Combat Training Battalion.

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:41.360
They're fine.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.390
Once they get it out of their 
system they'll calm down.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:49.150
What's her relationship with Yuuya?

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:55.440
Nobody move!

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:59.170
How did the MPs get here so fast?

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:00.650
No way.

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:03.000
Let's go, Lieutenant!

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.720
But what about Yuuya and Leon?

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:06.670
They're both used to it.

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:08.400
Hey, wait.

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:09.430
Used to it?

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:10.410
We're running.

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:11.680
Hurry!

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:13.680
There they go! That way!

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:16.180
Yuuya, we'll settle this...

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:18.190
During Blue Flag!

00:22:31.020 --> 00:22:33.530
Yuuya Bridges...

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:07.480
Can you imagine it?

00:24:07.480 --> 00:24:10.410
The heart of someone who's 
shunned just because they exist?

00:24:10.410 --> 00:24:11.790
I'll never forgive him for running away

00:24:11.790 --> 00:24:15.870
and leaving you, the captain, 
and everyone else behind.

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:20.430
Do you know what the opposite of "love" is?

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:24.310
<b>The Sound of Twisted Wings</b>

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:22.600
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:24.520
The Sound of Twisted Wings
